  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Friday)\nIssued at 126 PM CDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nSlightly warmer temperatures are expected Sunday, with most, if not \nall locations back in the lower to middle 70s. In summary. the \nweekend will be cool and dry with Fall in the air.\n\nNext week will feature a slow and steady warm-up, but the humidity \nshouldn't return to the level that it did earlier this week where we \nhad mornings in the mid to upper 70s. By mid to late week, \ntemperatures will warm back into the 80s with increasing \nsouthwesterly flow aloft as broad longwave troughing develops over \nthe western CONUS. This could set the stage for a stormier pattern \nby late week into next weekend, but it is still too far out to have \nmuch confidence on where any rain may fall.",
